---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About and disclosure"
  description="Who publishes Sorlio Guides, how the comparisons are written, and what we do and do not claim."
  path="/about/"
  current="about"
>
  <div class="prose-wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
    <h1>About Sorlio Guides</h1>
    <p class="lede">Sorlio Guides is a French-learning publication run by the makers of Sorlio.</p>

    <h2>Who publishes this site</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is published by the team that makes <strong>Sorlio</strong>, an Android app for learning French
      through reading. Because we make one of the apps we write about, we are not an independent review
      organisation, and we do not present our articles as impartial tests.
    </p>

    <h2>How comparison articles are written</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We describe other apps using their own public materials where we could check them, and we say where we could not.</li>
      <li>We do not invent user testimonials, ratings or test results. We have not published any measured learning outcomes.</li>
      <li>Where another product suits a learner better, the article says so.</li>
      <li>Prices, plans and features change. Check the product's own store page before you pay for anything.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Authors and review</h2>
    <p>
      Articles are written by the Sorlio team. We do not list individual author biographies or qualifications
      because none are claimed. Articles are not linguistically reviewed by a named native-speaker or teacher
      unless an article says so. Each guide shows its published and last-updated dates.
    </p>

    <h2>Google Play and privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Some links go to the <a href={SITE.playStoreUrl} rel="noopener">Sorlio listing on Google Play</a>. Sorlio is
      available for Android only. This site uses no advertising scripts, analytics trackers or consent banners.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial policy</h2>
    <p>How we choose topics, make comparisons, check facts and handle corrections is set out in our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>If something here is wrong or out of date, please tell us so we can correct it.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
